# REFERRAL APP — CURSOR RULES
# This file exists for backward compatibility.
# Primary instructions are in CLAUDE.md at the repo root.
# If using the Claude Code extension, CLAUDE.md takes priority.
# If using Cursor's built-in agent, this file applies.

Read CLAUDE.md for all project rules, architectural constraints, and workflow instructions.
Read PROGRESS.md before every task.

## Quick Reference (see CLAUDE.md for full details)

- TypeScript strict. No `any`, no `ts-ignore`.
- awardCredits()/deductCredits() are the ONLY credit modification paths.
- No SQL triggers. Application-layer logic only.
- SECURITY DEFINER → SET search_path = public.
- Append-only tables → REVOKE UPDATE/DELETE from all roles.
- Cron auth: Authorization: Bearer {CRON_SECRET} (not x-cron-secret).
- Atomic DB ops: single RPC/transaction, never sequential JS calls.
- Migrations: manual Supabase SQL editor, never supabase db push. Use CAST() not ::date.
- Admin client for writes, cookie-based client for reads.
- Game never imports from packages/api — API routes only.
- Package: @referral/api via transpilePackages.

## Prompt Format

Read .cursorrules first. [This is a code change task only — do not investigate.]
On branch [branch-name], [describe the change]:
1. [Specific change]
2. [Specific change]
[Constraints]
Commit and push to [branch-name] and open a PR.
